	I agree with the posters who indicate that the game is too hard.
	It really seems that there is something wrong with the attack /
	defense code.  Example:  Healer w/ AC 0 and 30 HP goes up against
	a monster with AC 3 and 20 HP and *loses* (wielding +1 short
	sword).  Or, as someone else indicated, a character with -6
	AC happening upon a soldier ant which takes one swipe at the
	guy (with full HP!) and he dies.  

	It seems to me, that without finding a wand of polymorph or
	a wand of wishing, there's no way to survive.  How many of you
	are really playing in non-wizard mode?  I don't know about you,
	but our version rarely ever has a wand of polymorph or a wand
	of wishing show up.  For that matter, since NH 2.3, the chance
	of finding shops has gone down drastically.  Also, where are 
	you all finding all these altars?  I've played several times
	down to level 8 to 10 and found at most one altar - almost
	always of the wrong alignment.  What happenned to good old
	Elbereth?  Seems that since 3.0, at least 50% of the time
	when you write it, the writing fails and the mosters destroy 
	you anyway.

	I think the biggest gripe we have is that things are thrown at
	you that there is no way to counter.  Most of the interesting 
	characters need armor FAST to even consider surviving.  The
	percentage of identify scrolls seems to have gone way down
	so you're forced to use items without knowing what they are.
	How do you survive when you put on a pair of cursed boots of
	levitation when you've never found a scroll of remove curse
	and your god is angry with you because you have on a helm of
	reverse alignment?  Is this stupidity?  I don't think so...
	I consider it a case of practicality.

	I'm not saying that the game should be a gimme, but we have
	experienced players here who have never gotten below level 10.
	The only thing I can think of is that there is either something
	wrong with the logic, or something wrong with the percentage
	chance of things, or something wrong with the way random
	numbers are generated.

